Appendix B: Full List of Assumptions

Assumption A1 (Feature sufficiency).
\mu_a(P) \perp P \mid \phi(P).

Assumption A2 (Linear expected costs).
\mu_a(x) = x^\top \theta_a with \|\theta_a\| \le S, \|x\| \le L.

Assumption A3 (Sub‑Gaussian noise).
C_t = x_t^\top \theta_{A_t} + \eta_t with \eta_t conditionally \sigma-sub‑Gaussian.

Assumption A4 (Prior structure).
\theta_a \sim \mathcal{N}(m_{0,a}, \frac{1}{\lambda} I_d) independently across arms, where m_{0,a} are derived from the LLM’s \pi_{\mathrm{LLM}} as described.

Assumption A5 (Bounded information ratio).
For the Gaussian linear prior and posterior, the Thompson sampling policy satisfies \Gamma_t \le K/2 for all t.

Assumption A6 (Initial calibration set).
An initial set of n i.i.d. labelled pairs (x_j, a^*(x_j)) from the initial distribution \mathcal{D}_0 is available. During the online phase, the true optimal arm for each round is eventually revealed (possibly with a bounded delay d).

