Appendix C: Proof of Theorem 1 (Long‑Run Coverage)

Statement. Under the adaptive update rule \alpha_{t+1} = \alpha_t + \gamma (\alpha - \mathrm{err}_t), for any sequence of errors \mathrm{err}_t \in \{0,1\},

\left| \frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^T \mathrm{err}_t - \alpha \right| \le \frac{1}{\gamma T} + \gamma.

Proof. Define the absolute loss \ell_t(\tilde{\alpha}) = |\tilde{\alpha} - \mathrm{err}_t|. The update can be seen as online subgradient descent on the sequence of loss functions f_t(\tilde{\alpha}) = \mathbb{E}[\ell_t(\tilde{\alpha})] but we work with actual realisations. A direct algebraic manipulation gives:

Let \bar{\mathrm{err}}_T = \frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^T \mathrm{err}_t. The ACI update implies that for any initial \alpha_1,

\alpha_{T+1} = \alpha_1 + \gamma \sum_{t=1}^T (\alpha - \mathrm{err}_t) = \alpha_1 + \gamma T(\alpha - \bar{\mathrm{err}}_T).

Since \alpha_{T+1} \in [0,1] (clipped if necessary), we have

|\alpha_1 + \gamma T(\alpha - \bar{\mathrm{err}}_T)| \le 1 \quad \Rightarrow \quad |\gamma T(\alpha - \bar{\mathrm{err}}_T)| \le 2.

Thus |\alpha - \bar{\mathrm{err}}_T| \le \frac{2}{\gamma T}. Moreover, by choosing \gamma = 1/\sqrt{T} we obtain \frac{1}{T}\sum_t \mathrm{err}_t \le \alpha + \frac{2}{\sqrt{T}}. ∎

The conformal set \mathcal{C}_t is constructed using the empirical quantile of the calibration window. The ACI only adjusts the target level \alpha_t; the quantile is computed from the stored scores. Because the calibration window size n is fixed and the scores are exchangeable within the window (assuming the window captures a locally stationary distribution), the basic coverage property still holds with the adjusted level, and the ACI theorem applies directly to the sequence of miscoverage errors \mathrm{err}_t. This yields the long‑run bound.

