Appendix G: Handling Delayed Truth Revelation

If the optimal arm a^*(x_t) is revealed with a delay of d rounds, the ACI update can be applied to the error \mathrm{err}_{t-d} once it becomes known. The miscoverage bound then becomes

\left| \frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^T \mathrm{err}_t - \alpha \right| \le \frac{1}{\gamma T} + \gamma + \frac{d}{T},

because the accumulation of delay induces at most d unrevealed errors at any time. The long‑run property is preserved; the additional term is \mathcal{O}(1/T).

